  "details": "A specific one of my avatars causes a crash every time. It is doing some major shader BS (specifically it does a chain of grabpass, then spit the result on the screen, then grabpass again several times for Jump Flood Algorithm outlines). Its been a long time since I worked on this avatar, so I don't remember any other shenanigans it does that could cause this crash. The last time I used this avatar (likely several months ago) it worked fine.\n\nRepro:\n\n1. Select the avatar in your menu so it loads as a preview or swap to the avatar\n\n2. Crash\n\nAvatar ID: avtr_cf3bc945-cb4b-4d11-8bdf-668efe558889\n\nNo crash dump gets generated that I could find. \n\nOutput log just has:\n\n2025.12.09 20:55:20 Debug      -  [AssetBundleDownloadManager] Starting download of 17 MB, 0 still queued.\n\n2025.12.09 20:55:20 Debug      -  [AssetBundleDownloadManager] [104] Unpacking Avatar (JFA DOG by Zеkk) \n\nthen nothing.",
